// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_extern_addr.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: the LINK-ASSERT phase reached through ONE ABSOLUTE ADDRESS under a bit
// operation — the third and last expression shape the `extern()` guard family uses.
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "LS16_EXTERN_ADDR_POISON: this poison claims EndOfRom is ODD; the
//                     link folds EndOfRom & 1 to 0"
//
// WHY A THIRD ROW. poison_extern_equate resolves an EQU, poison_extern_span subtracts two
// label VMAs; neither exercises a guard that reads ONE address and tests bits of it, which
// is the shape of:
//
//     engine/system/epilogue.emp:29        (extern("EndOfRom") & 1) == 0
//     engine/system/epilogue.emp:32        extern("EndOfRom") <= $3FFFFF
//     engine/objects/core.emp:63           (extern("Object_RAM_End") - extern("Object_RAM")) % 4 == 0
//     games/sonic4/player/player_common.emp:358
//                                          (extern("Player_1") & $FFFF8000) == $FFFF8000
//
// — the alignment and addressing-window class, where a silent drop would not shorten a
// buffer but would let a base land somewhere the code cannot address.
//
// WHY THE FRAGMENT'S 0 IS DERIVED AND NOT TYPED. It is epilogue.emp:29's OWN assertion:
// that guard says `(extern("EndOfRom") & 1) == 0` and fails the build with "ROM size is
// odd" if it ever stops holding. `emp_expect_fail` reads the `== <n>` out of that guard
// rather than typing 0, so the two move together — and if the ROM ever did become odd,
// epilogue.emp:29 fires first and this row's failure is a consequence, not a surprise.
//
// The poison's claim is therefore the exact negation of a guard the tree already enforces
// on every build, which is what makes it impossible to satisfy by accident: an edit that
// turned this poison green would have had to make the shipped ROM odd, and the shipped
// guard would have refused that edit first.
//
// Zero bytes, ensures-only — unreachable from any real entry.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_extern_addr

ensure((extern("EndOfRom") & 1) == 1, "LS16_EXTERN_ADDR_POISON: this poison claims EndOfRom is ODD; the link folds EndOfRom & 1 to {extern(\"EndOfRom\") & 1}")
